 "notes": "NASDUCK Floquet (Bloch et al., Sci.Adv. 2022). Main result: ALP-neutron coupling, Fig. 2, bright blue solid line (binned average / mean of the 95% C.L. bound). Curve recovered by vector extraction of the thin light-blue mean polyline (RGB 0.835,0.906,0.988) from the vector PDF; axes calibrated from tick marks (x: m_DM decades at 10^-14,-13,-12; y: g_aNN decades). Paper plots g_aNN in GeV^-1 defined via L = g_aNN d_mu a N-bar gamma^mu gamma5 N (Eqs 1-2). Applied 2m_N rule: g_an(dimensionless) = 2 m_n g_aNN[GeV^-1], m_n=0.9396 GeV, factor 1.879. DM density rho=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (not rescaled). Mass range ~4e-15 to 4e-12 eV. Local-median sampling used to suppress single-frequency spikes in the dense-measurement mean line. Main ALP-neutron (linear) result chosen over quadratic (Fig 3) and model-dependent proton bounds.",
